    {
      "id": "claim_9cf88ecc492d480b9b3c8c3d4459fcc5",
      "statement": "The MCP server is per-invocation and must not hold approval state; pending actions and session grants live only in extension background memory (a Set), are never persisted to page localStorage, extension storage, or IndexedDB, and are cleared on bridge disconnect, extension reload, or session end, keeping MCP stateless across invocations while the extension and relay are the continuity boundary.",
